flowchart TD
  accTitle: Eventology architecture
  accDescr: The Next.js web app and the Expo mobile app share packages for schemas, locales, config, utilities, AI and wallet passes. Both call public read routes and protected routes. Protected routes turn the better-auth session into a signed Supabase JWT, so Row Level Security applies in Supabase PostgreSQL. Payments, email, SMS, push, AI and wallet passes sit behind provider seams that default to stubs.

  shared["Shared packages: schemas, locales, config, utils, AI, wallet"]
  shared -.-> web["Web app: Next.js 16"]
  shared -.-> mobile["Mobile app: Expo SDK 54"]
  web --> pub["Public API: read only"]
  mobile --> pub
  web --> prot["Protected API"]
  mobile --> prot
  prot -- better-auth session to signed Supabase JWT --> db[("Supabase PostgreSQL: RLS, PostGIS, Realtime, Storage")]
  pub --> db
  prot --> seams["Provider seams: payments, email, SMS, push, AI, wallet"]
